    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 20,
        "line": 4,
        "text": "If I spoke about it- If I did- what would I tell you, I wonder? Would I tell you about the time...? It happened a long time ago- in the last days of a fair Prince’s reign... Or would I tell you about the place? A small city near the coast but far from everything else..."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 20,
        "line": 670,
        "text": "But when I think of her, of Elisa- all that comes to mind is a poem. Made of just a few truthful words... Whispered by someone in love, hundreds of years ago... “Unable to perceive the shape of You, I find You all around me."
      }
